# The batch 78 to 97

Twenty degrees at once.  `Sendov.R_le_batch` bounds every `R n α` for `78 ≤ n ≤ 97` by the
elementary part and moment at `n₀ = 78` together with the prefactor at `n₁ = 97`, so one
moment and one certificate serve all twenty.  The certificate has degree 76, set by `n₀`
rather than `n₁`, so it is cheaper than any single degree in the batch except the first.

Feasibility at `n₀` is not assumed: for `n ≥ 36` it follows from `0 ≤ α ≤ 17`, since
`A - c²` increases with `n` and is already nonnegative at `n = 78`.
-/

